XHTTP client: fix the WaitReadCloser data race, the closed flag race and the upload byte count race

Upstream: 77f98eba0978cbcb425e2f8ec3cec86bd5aa8444
Upstream: eef6e63bc16d6e97fd98178556d49aad7978809a

Backport: every changed line of client.go and dialer.go is upstream code, unchanged. Only the hunk context
differs from upstream, because the pin does not carry 986c512 (request creation error), 9d9eaf3 (closing the
stream-up body) or 1e036ce (closing the HTTP/3 transport). They are not part of this port: 986c512 and 9d9eaf3
keep their own pending waivers, and 1e036ce matches no drift keyword and comes with the pin move.
client_race_test.go is fork code. It holds a -race test for each of the three races, and an interleaving
test that runs stream-down, early-close, failed, stream-up and packet-up requests at once on one client.
That test checks that each stream reads exactly its own body, that a stream closed early never reads foreign
data, and that every response body is closed exactly once. The same races also failed upstream's
TestDialWithRemoteAddr and the splithttp TestTrustedHeaderScenarios under -race.

